---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="CLAAS Hydraulic Quick Couplers | Hydraulic Quick Couplings" description="Hydraulic quick couplers for CLAAS machines — ISO 7241 / ISO 16028 flat-face / ISO 5675 profiles, sizes, threads and selection notes for CLAAS fleets.">
  <section class="bg-navy-950 text-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-night-green">Machine-Compatible Quick Couplings</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight">CLAAS Hydraulic Quick Couplers</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-lg text-slate-300">Source the right quick-disconnect couplings for CLAAS machines — attachment lines, implement outlets and service replacements.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:font-extrabold prose-headings:text-navy-950 prose-h2:mt-10 prose-p:text-slate-600 prose-a:text-brand-blue">
        <h2>CLAAS Machines and Their Hydraulic Quick Couplings</h2>
        <p>CLAAS builds combine harvesters, forage harvesters, balers and tractors for arable and forage farming. CLAAS tractor rear outlets and implement lines use ISO 5675 agricultural couplings; newer loader and auxiliary circuits may use ISO 7241 ball-lock or flat-face depending on configuration.</p>
        <h2>Coupling Profiles You Will Find on CLAAS Equipment</h2>
        <p>The table below summarises the quick-coupling profiles most commonly used across CLAAS machine families. It is a field guide, not a guarantee: verify the profile on your specific machine before ordering.</p>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Machine family</th><th>Common profile</th><th>Typical sizes</th><th>Typical threads</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Tractor rear outlets</td><td>ISO 5675 (agricultural)</td><td>1/2&quot; ISO 5675</td><td>BSPP / NPT</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Loader / auxiliary lines</td><td>Ball-lock ISO 7241 or flat-face</td><td>1/2&quot; - 3/4&quot;</td><td>BSPP / NPT</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Service lines</td><td>Ball-lock ISO 7241</td><td>1/2&quot; - 3/4&quot;</td><td>BSPP / NPT</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <h2>Selection Notes for CLAAS Fleets</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>CLAAS tractor and implement outlets are ISO 5675 — the agricultural standard.</li><li>European-built CLAAS machines typically use BSPP threads; confirm per machine.</li><li>Forage harvester and baler lines vary by model year — check the coupling face before ordering.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Replacement and Service Guidance</h2>
        <p>CLAAS machines are predominantly European-market builds with BSPP threads. Provide the machine model and a photo of the coupling halves for an accurate profile match.</p>
        <h2>FAQ</h2>
        <h3>Do CLAAS tractors use ISO 5675?</h3><p>Yes — CLAAS tractor rear outlets use ISO 5675 agricultural couplings.</p><h3>What threads on CLAAS machines?</h3><p>European-built CLAAS machines typically use BSPP threads; export machines vary.</p><h3>Are CLAAS implement couplings standard?</h3><p>Yes — CLAAS implements use industry-standard ISO 5675 or ISO 7241 profiles.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-slate-50">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
      <div class="flex flex-col items-center justify-between gap-6 rounded-2xl bg-navy-950 p-8 text-center sm:p-10 lg:flex-row lg:text-left">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-white">Need Couplings for CLAAS Machines?</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-slate-300">Send the machine model, coupling profile or a photo — we confirm the match within 24 hours.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact/" class="rounded-lg bg-cta-orange px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-orange-600">Request a Quote</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
